    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What would you do if you loved something very much but found it too hard—perhaps even impossible—to develop "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "professionally",
            "ref": "v-professionally"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and shine on a big stage?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "That was the question Zhang Xue faced in 2006. At the time, the 19-year-old was earning a living as a motorcycle mechanic in Hunan. He had spent over three years learning to repair motorcycles and perform stunts. Despite his passion, he was too poor to take his skills to the next level. Hoping to join a racing team, Zhang asked a provincial news programme for a chance to appear on TV. But when the camera was pointed at him, his performance was hardly satisfying. The journalist naturally refused his request for another chance."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Zhang, however, wasn’t ready to give up. He rode more than 100 kilometres in the rain on his old, rusty motorcycle to chase down the production team. When asked why he was so determined, he replied, “If you never take action when you’re young, you’ll regret it when you’re old. But if you try, even failure brings no regret.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Now 39, Zhang has no reason to regret his choice. Instead, he can look back on that day in 2006 with pride."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "On March 28, the second round of the 2026 "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Supersport World Championship",
            "zh": "世界超级摩托车锦标赛"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " was held in Portugal. When French motorcyclist Valentin Debise crossed the finish line first, Zhang jumped to his feet. Winners of the series usually ride bikes from international brands like Yamaha. Debise, however, was riding a ZXMoto, a brand founded by Zhang. His victory marked the first Supersport World Championship win for a Chinese manufacturer. “I’m at a loss for words,” Zhang wrote on Douyin."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "After the 2006 "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "feature",
            "zh": "专题节目"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "aired",
            "ref": "v-air"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", Zhang joined a racing team as a rider and mechanic before becoming a motorcycle engineer. Step by step, he turned his passion into a career by modifying and selling bikes. In 2017, Zhang and his partners founded their first motorcycle brand, Kove Moto. Then, in 2024, he left Kove to start ZXMoto."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "“I never thought about doing anything else,” Zhang said after the recent win. “I simply love motorcycles.”"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "What would your answer be to the question at the beginning of this article? Would you follow Zhang’s example and go all out for what you love?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
